# {{ template "chart.name" . }}

{{ template "chart.description" . }} Pulls from Docker Hub, gcr.io, ghcr.io, registry.k8s.io, quay.io and any registry you add, through one host name or one per upstream, without writing image layers to disk.

{{ template "chart.homepageLine" . }}

## Install

```bash
kubectl create namespace registry-mirror
# The first administrator: there is no default password
openssl rand -base64 18 > admin-password
kubectl -n registry-mirror create secret generic registry-mirrors-relay-admin --from-file=password=admin-password

helm install registry-mirrors-relay oci://ghcr.io/openlinkos/charts/registry-mirrors-relay \
  --namespace registry-mirror --version {{ template "chart.version" . }} \
  --set admin.existingSecret=registry-mirrors-relay-admin
```

Open the admin console with `kubectl -n registry-mirror port-forward svc/registry-mirrors-relay 8080:80` and `http://127.0.0.1:8080/admin/`.

## Admin console, admin API and metrics

They share the pull port by default and answer only direct connections from loopback and private addresses (`config.admin.allow`): `kubectl port-forward` and Prometheus scraping the pods work, while anything that comes through an Ingress, a Gateway or a CDN carries forwarding headers and gets 404. Metrics are off unless `metrics.enabled` or `metrics.serviceMonitor.enabled`.

Set `admin.separatePort: true` to move all three to their own port and `<fullname>-admin` Service instead. A NodePort or LoadBalancer pull Service needs either that or `service.externalTrafficPolicy: Local`, because otherwise outside clients arrive with node addresses and look internal; the chart refuses to render the combination.

## Modes

- `mode: readonly` (default): a Deployment with two replicas and a PodDisruptionBudget. Operational data (accounts, IP and image rules, bans) comes only from `config`; the console shows it read-only. The first administrator from `admin.existingSecret` is the only one and its password stays valid, so keep it long and random.
- `mode: writable`: a StatefulSet with one replica and a PersistentVolumeClaim for the operational database. The console can create accounts, rules and bans, and change entrances, upstreams, rate limits and the cache on top of `config`; those changes live on the PVC and are invisible to `helm upgrade` and GitOps tools, so set `config.admin.config_edit: false` if values must decide everything. The first administrator must change the password at the first sign-in; afterwards the Secret can be deleted.

## Configuration

`config` is the relay configuration (see [config.example.yaml](https://github.com/openlinkos/registry-mirrors-relay/blob/main/config.example.yaml)) and is rendered into a ConfigMap. The chart sets `data_dir`, `listen`, `admin.store` and `metrics.enabled` itself, and rejects `tls` and secrets written as `value`: mount secrets and reference them with `env` or `file`.

```yaml
config:
  client_ip:
    trusted_proxies: [10.42.0.0/16]   # your ingress controller's pod network
  entrances:
    - name: mirror
      hosts: [mirror.example.com]
ingress:
  enabled: true
  className: traefik
  hosts:
    - host: mirror.example.com
  tls:
    - hosts: [mirror.example.com]
      secretName: mirror-example-com-tls
```

To let containerd on the nodes pull through the relay, expose it on an address the nodes can reach (`service.type: NodePort` or `LoadBalancer`, or the Ingress host) and write `/etc/containerd/certs.d/<upstream>/hosts.toml`; see the [deployment guide](https://github.com/openlinkos/registry-mirrors-relay/blob/main/docs/deploy.en.md).

## Verify

The chart is signed keylessly by this repository's release workflow and has a build provenance attestation:

```bash
cosign verify ghcr.io/openlinkos/charts/registry-mirrors-relay:{{ template "chart.version" . }} \
  --certificate-identity-regexp '^https://github.com/openlinkos/registry-mirrors-relay/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/tags/v' \
  --certificate-oidc-issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com
gh attestation verify oci://ghcr.io/openlinkos/charts/registry-mirrors-relay:{{ template "chart.version" . }} -R openlinkos/registry-mirrors-relay
```

